<h2>1. About ArenaX</h2>
<p>
ArenaX is a gaming and social media platform where users can
create profiles, share gaming-related posts, upload images,
and interact with other members of the gaming community.
ArenaX is intended for users aged 14 and above.
</p>

<h2>2. Zero-Tolerance Policy Against CSAE</h2>
<p>
ArenaX has zero tolerance for Child Sexual Abuse and Exploitation
(CSAE). Any content or behaviour that sexually exploits, abuses,
grooms, threatens, or endangers minors is strictly prohibited.
</p>
<p>
Users must not create, upload, share, request, or distribute
Child Sexual Abuse Material (CSAM) through ArenaX.
Such content is prohibited regardless of whether it is presented
as a photograph, video, illustration, or other media.
</p>

<h2>3. Prohibited Activities</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Sharing or distributing CSAM.</li>
    <li>Sexual exploitation or grooming of minors.</li>
    <li>Sexual threats, sextortion, or blackmail involving minors.</li>
    <li>Soliciting sexual images or personal information from minors.</li>
    <li>Harassment, abuse, or threats directed at minors.</li>
    <li>Content that encourages or facilitates child exploitation.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Reporting Child Safety Concerns</h2>
<p>
Users can report inappropriate content, accounts, or behaviour
through the reporting features available within ArenaX.
Users can also contact our child safety team directly by email:
</p>
<p>
<strong>Email:</strong>
<a href="mailto:pankajsharma200051@gmail.com">
pankajsharma200051@gmail.com
</a>
</p>
<p>
Reports should include relevant details about the account or
content involved. Please do not download, forward, or redistribute
suspected CSAM as evidence.
</p>

<h2>5. Moderation and Enforcement</h2>
<p>
ArenaX reviews child safety reports and takes appropriate action
when violations are identified. Actions may include:
</p>
<ul>
    <li>Removing prohibited content.</li>
    <li>Restricting or suspending violating accounts.</li>
    <li>Terminating accounts involved in serious violations.</li>
    <li>Taking appropriate action under applicable laws.</li>
</ul>
<p>
ArenaX does not tolerate the creation, storage, or distribution
of CSAM on its platform. We take appropriate action when we
obtain actual knowledge of such material.
</p>

<h2>6. Compliance With Child Safety Laws</h2>
<p>
ArenaX is committed to complying with applicable child safety
laws and regulations. Confirmed cases of child sexual abuse
material will be handled in accordance with applicable legal
requirements, including reporting to the relevant regional
or national authorities where required.
</p>

